# D31: npm package ships only genesis genes (rotifer init needs them).
# All other genes are available via Rotifer Cloud (D1: Cloud-Centric Gene ecosystem).
# Package policy: ship only genesis genes in the npm tarball.

# Default: exclude everything
*

# Keep genesis genes required by `rotifer init` (resolveGenesisDir)
!genesis-web-search/
!genesis-web-search/**
!genesis-web-search-lite/
!genesis-web-search-lite/**
!genesis-file-read/
!genesis-file-read/**
!genesis-code-format/
!genesis-code-format/**
!genesis-l0-constraint/
!genesis-l0-constraint/**

# `hello --template quality-advisor` — the first command the README and the
# init banner recommend — runs gene-health-scanner, and `init` copies it from
# here (RECOMMENDED_TEMPLATE_GENES). Leaving it out broke that first run on
# every published version from 0.30.0 to 0.30.2 (#453).
# scripts/smoke-packed-package.sh fails if a gene init copies is missing.
!gene-health-scanner/
!gene-health-scanner/**
